WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.303
-My next guest is a dancer,
singer, actress,

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.405
and social-media superstar.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.206
I mean, seriously superstar.

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:11.310
She has 32 million followers
on TikTok

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.281
and over 12 million subscribers
on her YouTube channel.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.916
She works hard.
She deserves it.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.018
She's currently working
on a new project

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.220
that she is announcing tonight.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.524
I can't wait.
Here is Jojo Siwa!

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.759
-Hey!
I'm so excited!

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.727
Thank you for having me.
-Welcome back.

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:29.929
Thanks for being here.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.265
I know it's over zoom,
but we appreciate it.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:36.535
We have so much to talk about.
-We do.

00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:38.037
-One of the things
I love about you

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.440
and your fans love about you
is that you are always yourself.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.976
You're always you.
-Yes.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:45.578
-And you're always leading
by example

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:49.014
and spreading positivity,
very positive.

00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:50.349
-Thank you.
-And you continue to do that

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:54.453
now more than ever.
Two weeks ago, you posted this.

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:59.059
You opened up about being
part of the LGBTQ community,

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.826
and immediately,
love started pouring in

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:03.362
from all over the world.
How does it feel?

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.097
Where were you in your head
at the time?

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:11.303
-It was the most
insane thing ever.

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:14.340
I mean, literally everyone
and their brother messaged me,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.444
called me, texted me, sent me an
Instagram message, tweeted me.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:21.280
It was the most love, I think,
I've ever received,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.684
and the coolest thing about it
was it was just by me

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.519
showing the world
the last little piece of me

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:29.155
that they haven't seen yet,
and it was really awesome.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.257
-Did you plan on doing it?

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.958
-So, that's actually
what's funny about it.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:36.729
So, I was doing TikToks
with the people

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:37.930
who are in the Pride House.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.665
That's, like, what their
TikTok house is called,

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:41.834
is the Pride House.
And I love them.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.670
I've known them all for years,
and so we were like,

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.971
"Let's just do
some TikToks together

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.306
before I leave for Canada."
And they come over,

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.208
and we're doing this TikTok,
and I was like,

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:52.278
"I think this TikTok that we're
doing to 'Ain't It Fun,'"

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.914
I was like, "I think this is
gonna out me."

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:58.550
And I was like, "I don't really
mind, because it is true."

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:02.822
I do have the most amazing,
wonderful, perfect

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.925
most beautiful girlfriend
in the whole world.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.593
It's not something
I'm ashamed of.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.663
I just haven't shown
the Internet yet.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.565
And there's always been
speculations, of course,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.733
but so then I was like,
"I think this is gonna out me."

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:16.668
So then I posted that --
they posted that,

00:02:16.668 --> 00:02:19.672
and, of course, it did,
and people started commenting --

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.108
and people started commenting to
me, "Is this you coming out?

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.143
Like, is this you coming out?
What is this? What is this?"

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:25.578
So I was like,
"You know what I can do?

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:29.315
I can either mess with them
and, like, tease a little bit,

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.451
I could either confirm it,
because it is true,

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.485
or I can just kind of
do nothing about it

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:35.154
and just kind of
leave it there."

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.123
And I was like, "I want to do a
TikTok to 'Born This Way.'"

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.224
'Cause it is true.
I don't really want to be like,

00:02:39.224 --> 00:02:41.160
"Yeah, it's true," right away,
but I was like,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.962
"I want people to know that,
like, it's okay."

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.730
So I did this TikTok
to "Born This Way,"

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.166
and everyone was like, "Whoa!
This is her coming out!

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:49.134
This is her coming out!
This is the moment!"

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:51.271
And I was like, "I..."

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.873
And then, my cousin
had gotten me that shirt.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.575
I took that picture
like a week before

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:58.144
I posted it,
and I actually -- I put it on

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.979
my close friend's
Instagram story,

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.381
and all my friends know,
all my family knows.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:05.018
And then, one day, I was
on FaceTime with my girlfriend.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:08.220
This is the day after I posted
the "Born This Way" TikTok.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.056
And I was on FaceTime with her,
and we were just

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.758
talking about it
and talking about all the love

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.592
that came in,
and we were both like,

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:16.663
"Technically, I still haven't
confirmed it."

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:18.597
And so I was like,
"I kind of want to post

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.332
this picture on my real story."

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:22.835
And she was super encouraging.
She was like, "Do it."

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:26.205
and I was like, "All right!"
And I did it.

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:29.274
And the funny thing is,
is 10 minutes before I did that,

00:03:29.274 --> 00:03:31.544
you can only imagine the
press storm that was happening.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.546
I mean, it was insane.
-Yeah.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.482
And 10 minutes before I posted
that, my publicist was like,

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.383
"So, are you gonna confirm it?"
and I was like,

00:03:38.383 --> 00:03:39.919
"No, I'm not gonna
confirm it yet."

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.455
10 minutes later, I post that
picture and start texting her.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:45.424
I was like, "Hey.
So about not confirming it,

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:46.725
go look at my story."
-"It's out."

00:03:46.725 --> 00:03:49.328
Did you -- Did you --
Did you put your phone down?

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:51.697
Because you probably go like...

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.265
Either way,
you're gonna get feedback.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:54.867
You're gonna get good stuff,
and you're gonna get bad stuff.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.135
-Totally.
-And you know it's gonna

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.703
start a conversation.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.703 --> 00:04:01.473
-And you're like,
"Once I press this button..."

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:04.010
-There's no going back.
-Yes.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.979
-My thing with "coming out" is

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.848
it can be a very scary thing,
you know?

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.616
Of course not everybody
in the world is going to

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:13.085
accept it right now,
but there are so many people

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:15.287
that are going
to accept it right now.

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:17.757
And like I say, even if there's
a million people --

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.391
say there's a million people --
that's a lot of people

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:23.029
that don't accept it,
there's 100 million that do.

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.964
And I think that's something
really important.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:29.067
100 million is a lot of people,
and so always keep that in mind.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:31.970
But, also, I was like,
"I don't want it to have to be

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.307
such a big thing."
Like, what am I gonna do?

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:37.242
Like, have a coming-out party?
No, it's just who I am.

00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:40.179
And so, after I posted it,
I was just kind of like,

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.948
"All right! I'll do it." Like,
I was on the phone spontaneous,

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:44.750
like, 'cause she --
we're long-distance,

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.018
and so I was like,
"All right, I did it."

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:49.255
Back to FaceTiming with her.
And then it was like

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.557
two days later,
I was again on the phone.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.326
We're on the phone
literally 24/7.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:56.395
Both of our families get so
annoyed at us, but it's okay.

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:59.164
It doesn't matter.
But I was like,

00:04:59.164 --> 00:05:02.702
"You know what I realized?
How risky that was."

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.003
And she was like,
"Well, what do you mean?"

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.837
And I was like,
"Well, technically,

00:05:05.837 --> 00:05:08.707
that was a really big risk
that I took posting that."

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:10.509
But I was like,
"But honestly --"

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:12.245
And she's like, "Why? Because
you could've lost everything?"

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:15.348
And I was like, "Yeah.
But if I lost everything

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:19.485
that I've created
because of being myself

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.420
and because of loving
who I want to love,

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.257
I don't want it.
That's not what I want

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.525
if I can't love
who I want to love."

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:28.561
That's one of the most
important things to me.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.930
And it was about 10 minutes
before I came out

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:34.701
to do this interview today,
I was again on the phone

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:38.604
with my girl,
and I started crying.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.239
And she's like,
"What's wrong with you?"

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.807
And I was like,
"I'm just so happy."

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:45.011
I was like, "Because now
I get to share

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:47.480
what makes me the happiest
with the world,

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.815
and it makes my heart so happy."

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:52.518
-There's a lot
to be happy about.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.754
I want to congratulate you,
because you were named

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:59.558
one of Time Magazine's 100 Most
Influential People of 2020.

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:02.161
Now, you are 17 years old

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.897
and one of the most influential
people on the planet.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:06.899
-Crazy.
-How does it feel,

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:10.135
and do you feel different?
-Isn't that crazy?

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:12.404
I mean, it is insane.

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:17.110
I don't feel different.
I mean, nothing changed,

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:22.314
but I guess I didn't really
realize what a big deal it was

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:24.016
until I actually saw the list

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.951
and saw the other people
that were on it,

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:30.555
and then I was like, "Whoa.
Like, this is a huge honor."

00:06:30.555 --> 00:06:32.658
And, I mean, it's insane,

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.727
and I'm so thankful,
and I'm so grateful.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.995
Actually, something funny
that came from it is,

00:06:36.995 --> 00:06:39.832
we created a new game in my
family and my close friends.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.301
So, my best friend, Nate,
we made a game

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.036
where I try to influence people
to do something.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:45.471
And it's the smallest things.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:48.173
So, say we have a whole bunch
of pizzas, and I'll be like,

00:06:48.173 --> 00:06:49.308
to somebody, I'll be like,
"Oh, my gosh.

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:51.143
Yeah, the cheese is good,
but the pepperoni,

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:52.578
you gotta try the pepperoni."

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.546
And if I get them to do it,
Nate and I look at each other,

00:06:54.546 --> 00:06:57.850
and we're like,
"Time 100, baby!

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.052
Up top!"
-"That's how influential I am.

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:03.188
Look at how influential --
He doesn't even like pepperoni."

00:07:03.188 --> 00:07:05.858
-We try.
We try so hard, and it works.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:08.427
And it's -- well, all the time,
we're like, "Top 100, baby.

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:11.631
That's me."
-Yeah. Why not?

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.932
I saw you did something
over quarantine,

00:07:13.932 --> 00:07:17.670
because obviously, we all had
to cut the tours short

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:22.708
and all this no live events,
and, you know, you --

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:25.243
when you're a performer,
you have to perform.

00:07:25.243 --> 00:07:28.280
We've had people on the show,
comedians going like,

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.649
"I just miss it.
I have to.

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:32.518
It's part of me."
-Yeah.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.786
-And you did something
very cool.

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:36.422
You built a stage
in your backyard.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:41.393
-I did, I did.
So, my mom was watching people

00:07:41.393 --> 00:07:43.128
perform, like,
from their living room,

00:07:43.128 --> 00:07:45.631
and I was watching people
perform from their couch.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:50.102
And I was like,
"I want to see a concert."

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:53.005
And my mom was like,
"You should do one of these."

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:54.573
So, that was kind of
where it came from, from me.

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:55.741
I was like, "I want to do one."

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.743
And my mom was like,
"You should do one."

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:00.012
And I was like,
"But I -- I can't."

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:02.381
I was like, "I can't sit
on my couch and sing a song.

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.616
It just doesn't --
It doesn't work."

00:08:04.616 --> 00:08:07.653
Like, I literally
don't know how to do that.

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:10.189
I say all the time, "I'm an
Ameri-can, not an Ameri-can't,"

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:12.224
but, like, I can't do that.

00:08:12.224 --> 00:08:15.527
And she was -- she was like,
"So then don't."

00:08:15.527 --> 00:08:17.529
She was like, "Build a stage."

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:20.298
And I was like,
"Well, all right."

00:08:20.298 --> 00:08:23.402
And so I started looking
on Amazon, and I was like,

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:25.504
"All right," I have
these platforms in my cart,

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:27.406
and I was just gonna, like,
do it for one week.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:29.107
And then I was like,
"This still doesn't feel right."

00:08:29.107 --> 00:08:32.344
So I message my friend who
kind of just can do anything.

00:08:32.344 --> 00:08:33.945
And I was like, "Hey.

00:08:33.945 --> 00:08:36.082
Do you have a guy that could
help me build a stage?"

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:37.850
And she was like,
"Yeah, let me get on it."

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.019
-[ Laughs ]
I love it. Two seconds --

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:41.821
"Yeah. Of course."
-Two seconds.

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.356
She was like,
"Yeah, yeah, totally."

00:08:43.356 --> 00:08:47.159
And so now it turned into
this whole thing,

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:48.994
and it's so awesome,
and it's so incredible.

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:50.730
I did it every Friday.
I think I did --

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.365
I think I did 12 of them and
then a few dance videos, too,

00:08:53.365 --> 00:08:54.966
and it was just so much fun,
you know?

00:08:54.966 --> 00:08:58.204
And we put on full-blown shows
of singing and dancing

00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:00.906
and lights and music
and a stage and costumes.

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:03.442
-Good for you.
-And it was just --

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:06.845
It kept me so happy.
We would shoot, like,

00:09:06.845 --> 00:09:10.316
three of them in a week,
and it just, that week,

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:12.217
I was always the happiest human.

00:09:12.217 --> 00:09:14.186
-Speaking of costumes,

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:18.290
you have one of the biggest
empires of consumer products.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.392
I told you my girls
are fans of yours,

00:09:20.392 --> 00:09:22.661
and so we have
bows all over the house,

00:09:22.661 --> 00:09:24.930
we have headphones
with bows on them, we have --

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.433
Your books, by the way,
are fantastic.

00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:29.635
-I love it.
-We -- It's just --

00:09:29.635 --> 00:09:32.604
I think they kind of
started writing diaries.

00:09:32.604 --> 00:09:34.506
But I think I've read somewhere

00:09:34.506 --> 00:09:38.644
you've sold over
80 million hair bows.

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:40.980
Is that wild?
-It's crazy.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:44.349
It's so incredible.
I'm so thankful.

00:09:44.349 --> 00:09:47.419
I mean, my mom and I
actually have been selling bows

00:09:47.419 --> 00:09:49.654
for much longer
than people think.

00:09:49.654 --> 00:09:50.990
I'll never forget when I was --

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.691
I think I would've been
5 years old --

00:09:52.691 --> 00:09:56.595
4 or 5 years old --
we used to go to our local,

00:09:56.595 --> 00:09:59.097
you know, haircut places
or little boutique stores,

00:09:59.097 --> 00:10:00.833
and my mom told me, she was
like, "Here, you carry them,

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:02.101
'cause you're cute and little,

00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:03.335
and they'll want to buy it
from you."

00:10:03.335 --> 00:10:04.970
And I was like, "Okay!"
So, we're walking in

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.006
with our little basket of bows.

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:09.708
And we tell the people, "Hey,
do you want to buy some bows?"

00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:11.711
And this one time, they're like,
"Yeah, we'll buy it.

00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:14.013
We'll buy 10 of them."
And my mom and I,

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:15.381
we were, like, so pumped up.

00:10:15.381 --> 00:10:16.815
We walk out of there
with 100 bucks,

00:10:16.815 --> 00:10:18.150
we're like,
"We're going shopping!

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.052
We're going to lunch,
we're going shopping!

00:10:20.052 --> 00:10:21.854
It's gonna be
the best day ever!"

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:25.123
And so now to think that
that 10 bows

00:10:25.123 --> 00:10:29.328
has translated into 80 million,

00:10:29.328 --> 00:10:33.566
I mean, that is insane
and amazing,

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:36.668
and I'm so thankful
and so grateful.

00:10:36.668 --> 00:10:38.504
Because of what
the bow stands for, you know,

00:10:38.504 --> 00:10:40.372
being yourself,
being kind to everybody,

00:10:40.372 --> 00:10:43.575
to think that there's
80 million of them out there,

00:10:43.575 --> 00:10:46.746
it just --
it makes my heart so happy.

00:10:46.746 --> 00:10:49.715
-You've accomplished so much,
and you're still a teenager.

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:51.750
What would you say
is your ultimate dream

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.652
or another dream, another goal?

00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:57.589
Something you haven't done yet
but you know one day you'll do.

00:10:57.589 --> 00:11:00.659
-Oh, man.
I -- Yeah.

00:11:00.659 --> 00:11:03.695
My biggest dream, and it's
coming up this weekend,

00:11:03.695 --> 00:11:05.598
is to play the Super Bowl,
to do the halftime show

00:11:05.598 --> 00:11:06.832
at the Super Bowl.

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:09.101
I have seen
every single one of them.

00:11:09.101 --> 00:11:11.369
I mean, from Jackson --

00:11:11.369 --> 00:11:12.838
Michael Jackson's
Super Bowl show

00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:14.507
to Gaga's Super Bowl show,

00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:16.308
I think is probably
my all-time favorite.

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:17.977
J.Lo's incredible.

00:11:17.977 --> 00:11:20.012
I can't wait to see
The Weeknd this year.

00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:23.182
-Let's get him on the phone.
We can get you --

00:11:23.182 --> 00:11:25.117
The Weeknd --
Let me call The Weeknd.

00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:27.319
-Beep boop boop!
-Yeah, I'll call The Weeknd,

00:11:27.319 --> 00:11:29.454
we'll get you a private plane
to Tampa, and --

00:11:29.454 --> 00:11:31.223
-Tell him I'll do a little
"Blinding Lights"

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:33.292
for him on stage.
I got it. I got the TikTok.

00:11:33.292 --> 00:11:34.893
I got it.
Let's go.

00:11:34.893 --> 00:11:36.762
-Yeah. Of course, yeah.
-Oh!

00:11:36.762 --> 00:11:38.831
-We can totally
get this happening.

00:11:38.831 --> 00:11:40.732
-Yeah.
-I can see you on that stage.

00:11:40.732 --> 00:11:42.301
That is --
-Thank you.

00:11:42.301 --> 00:11:43.735
-All right, let's put it
out there in the world.

00:11:43.735 --> 00:11:45.537
It's gonna happen.
-I'm a believer.

00:11:45.537 --> 00:11:48.106
I'm a "You believe it,
one day..."

00:11:48.106 --> 00:11:50.509
I might be 80 years old,
"Coming to you live

00:11:50.509 --> 00:11:52.912
from Jojo Siwa's death bed,
here we go!

00:11:52.912 --> 00:11:56.381
The Pepsi Halftime Show!"
[ Both laugh ]

00:11:56.381 --> 00:11:57.549
-You're wheeling out.

00:11:57.549 --> 00:11:58.951
You're still doing
"Blinding Light."

00:11:58.951 --> 00:12:01.720
♪ Do, do do ♪
"Yeah, that song is old now."

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:03.221
Yeah, we're...

00:12:03.221 --> 00:12:04.223
But you have a big --

00:12:04.223 --> 00:12:05.891
You have
a big announcement tonight.

00:12:05.891 --> 00:12:07.359
-I do.

00:12:07.359 --> 00:12:10.496
-Can you tell everyone where you
are and what you're working on?

00:12:10.496 --> 00:12:14.033
-So, I, right now,
am in Vancouver, Canada,

00:12:14.033 --> 00:12:17.703
and I am so excited, me and
my friends at Nickelodeon,

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:21.840
we are making a musical,
and I'm so pumped up about it.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.777
This musical
is centered around my life

00:12:24.777 --> 00:12:27.479
and also centered
around being yourself

00:12:27.479 --> 00:12:30.415
and centered around
staying true to who you are,

00:12:30.415 --> 00:12:32.951
and even when the world
is telling you

00:12:32.951 --> 00:12:34.753
that it's not gonna happen,
it's not gonna happen,

00:12:34.753 --> 00:12:36.755
you're believing
because you're you.

00:12:36.755 --> 00:12:38.723
And that's -- that's what
this movie is all about.

00:12:38.723 --> 00:12:41.594
And the music in it
I'm so happy about!

00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:45.163
I have worked
so hard on this soundtrack.

00:12:45.163 --> 00:12:48.000
There's six original songs
on the soundtrack

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.202
and then two of my old songs,

00:12:50.202 --> 00:12:52.972
but one of them
is like a full revamped --

00:12:52.972 --> 00:12:56.008
remix, and it's so much fun.

00:12:56.008 --> 00:12:59.878
But from the six original songs,
I created 27.

00:12:59.878 --> 00:13:02.547
Had to narrow it down to six.

00:13:02.547 --> 00:13:05.917
So it's been a process,
but it's been so much fun.

00:13:05.917 --> 00:13:08.587
Now that we're actually here,
it's happening,

00:13:08.587 --> 00:13:10.655
we've been in quarantine
in rehearsals.

00:13:10.655 --> 00:13:13.692
We have an incredible director.
We have an incredible writer.

00:13:13.692 --> 00:13:17.329
Obviously, my friends
at Nickelodeon, it's --

00:13:17.329 --> 00:13:19.364
Aah! I'm so excited!
-It sounds amazing.

00:13:19.364 --> 00:13:22.501
Do you have a title?
-We do. We do.

00:13:22.501 --> 00:13:24.769
It's called "The J-Team."
-"The J-Team"!

00:13:24.769 --> 00:13:28.006
I'm on The J-Team!
-You're on the J-Team!

00:13:28.006 --> 00:13:29.507
Jimmy's on the J-Team.
-That's you.

00:13:29.507 --> 00:13:32.410
-See, people think it stands
for The Jojo Team.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.313
It's really
the Jimmy Fallon Team.

00:13:34.313 --> 00:13:36.582
Don't let it fool you.
-That's what I'm talking about.

